 <juca@members.fsf.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:58:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] sr-aef: name an unnamed glyph as fontTools does

A glyph a font leaves unnamed (post format 3, or an empty post name) took
skrifa's made-up name, "gid94"; fontTools calls it "glyph00094". Tools that
pair a converted font's glyphs with the binary's by name then miss them: six
of Lato's unnamed glyphs, same outline and advance, found no counterpart. An
unnamed glyph is now "glyph" and its five-digit glyph id, as fontTools has it.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
---
 sr-aef/src/lib.rs | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sr-aef/src/lib.rs b/sr-aef/src/lib.rs
index 632791be..cfa143fd 100644
--- a/sr-aef/src/lib.rs
+++ b/sr-aef/src/lib.rs
@@ -1242,12 +1242,11 @@ pub fn unique_glyph_names(font: &skrifa::FontRef) -> Vec<SmolStr> {
     let stated: Vec<SmolStr> = (0..glyph_names.num_glyphs())
         .map(GlyphId::new)
         .map(|gid| {
-            SmolStr::new(
-                glyph_names
-                    .get(gid)
-                    .map(|s| s.to_string())
-                    .unwrap_or_else(|| format!("gid{:04}", gid)),
-            )
+            SmolStr::new(match glyph_names.get(gid) {
+                Some(name) if !name.is_synthesized() => name.to_string(),
+                // a glyph the font leaves unnamed, named as fontTools names it
+                _ => format!("glyph{:05}", gid.to_u32()),
+            })
         })
         .collect();
     unique_names(stated.iter().map(|name| fea_glyph_name(name)).collect())
